---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const LAST_UPDATED = '2026-07-08';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Affiliate Disclosure"
  description="How singletenant.ai marks referral links, which vendor relationships exist, and why commission never affects the data."
>
  <section>
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-12 md:py-16">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-3">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="m-0 mb-2" style="font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3.5vw, 2.5rem); letter-spacing: -0.02em;">
        Affiliate disclosure
      </h1>
      <p class="font-mono text-xs mb-10" style="color: var(--color-mute);">
        Last updated {LAST_UPDATED}
      </p>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Some outbound links on this site are referral links. If you follow
          one and become a customer of that vendor, this site may earn a
          commission. You pay nothing extra.
        </p>

        <h2>How referral links are marked</h2>
        <p>
          Every referral link is marked where it appears: a visible
          "Referral link" notice sits next to the link on the same page, and
          the link carries the <code>rel="sponsored"</code> attribute. If a
          link has no such notice, it is not a referral link. This page is
          linked from the notice and from the footer of every page.
        </p>

        <h2>Current relationships</h2>
        <p>
          This site has an affiliate relationship with <strong>RunPod</strong>.
          No other vendor in the database has a commercial relationship with
          this site. This list is updated whenever a relationship starts or
          ends, and the change is recorded in the
          <a href="/changelog/">changelog</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>What commission does not affect</h2>
        <p>
          Vendor facts on this site are verified against primary sources
          (vendor documentation, trust centres, and pricing pages), and every
          populated fact links to its evidence with the date it was checked.
          A fact that cannot be verified is shown as "Not verified"
          regardless of any commercial relationship. Commission does not
          determine which vendors are included, how they are ordered, or
          what the data says. The <a href="/methodology/">methodology
          page</a> describes the process.
        </p>

        <h2>Why this page exists</h2>
        <p>
          Identifying paid-for links is required by the UK CAP Code (enforced
          by the ASA) and, for US readers, the FTC's endorsement guides
          (16 CFR Part 255). Questions about this policy:
          <a href="mailto:editor@singletenant.ai">editor@singletenant.ai</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
